(54,61,NULL,'en','We depart from Quito in the morning and head south, driving through the famed ´´Avenue of the Volcanoes.´´ If the weather is good, we´ll see a number of snow-capped and glaciated peaks as we drive. After arriving at Cotopaxi National Park, our first stop is Limpiopungo Glacier Lake, located at the base of Volcan Rumiñahui. Limpiopungo is home to abundant highland waterfowl, and we´ll spot gulls, ducks, falcons, and more as we begin our hike. We also learn about the endemic paramo landscape, the unique tropical tundra endemic to the high northern Andes. Our path continues through the foothills of Rumiñahui and past several other small lakes and rivers. As we hike, we take in magnificent views of Cotopaxi´s massive, glaciated cone, looming over the high plain directly across from Rumiñahui. We also search for llamas, wild horses, deer, hares, and the endangered Andean Condor. After our hike, we refuel with a delicious, scenic picnic lunch. Finally, we visit the Pucara Inca ruins, where we learn about the Inca presence in Ecuador. We leave the park in the afternoon and head back to Quito. <br/><br/><b>INCLUDED\n</b><br/>Bilingual adventure guide, private transportation, nutritious picnic lunch and snacks.  <br/><br/><b>IMPORTANT INFORMATION\n</b><br/><b>TRAVEL TIME:</b> Two hours each way.\n<br/><b>HIKING TIME: </b>Three hours.\nSEASON: Year-round.\n<br/><b>ALTITUDE:</b> 3800 to 4200 meters\n(12,500 to 13,800 feet).\n<br/><b>SUGGESTED ITEMS TO PACK: </b>Layered clothing\nfor hot and cold weather, sunblock, gloves, boots, waterproof rain gear, hiking shoes, binoculars.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<br/>','jigranda','2016-08-24 11:22:56',NULL,NULL),
(57,64,NULL,'en','We head northwest from Quito, passing the equatorial monument and around the back side of Volcan Pichincha to reach the Mindo Cloud Forest Reserve. The climate here is much warmer than in Quito due to the lower altitude and coastal weather influence, creating a humid, subtropical cloud forest ecosystem that is home to a wide variety of unique flora and fauna. After a scenic drive to the town of Mindo and into the reserve, we begin a nature walk through this remarkable natural environment. As we hike, our naturalist guide identifies native species and teaches us the intricacies of the cloud forest ecosystem. Mindo is best known for its diverse bird life, and we comwill see scores of native birds, including cock-of-the-rocks, toucans, and more. We also observe a vast diversity of butterflies, orchids, and other native plants and animals. After our hike, we stop to visit the local waterfalls and enjoy a tasty lunch at a local restaurant before returning to Quito in the afternoon. <br/><br/><b>INCLUDED\n<br/></b>Private transportation, bilingual guide, and lunch. <br/><br/><b>NOT INCLUDED\n</b><br/>Restaurant beverages, and tips.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'<br/>','jigranda','2016-08-29 12:50:47',NULL,NULL),
(61,68,NULL,'en','We take an early flight from Quito to Cuenca,\ntouching down in just over 45 minutes. Upon\narrival, we check in to our boutique hotel in\nCuenca´s old town and get ready to explore the\narea by bike. We start riding through Cuenca´s\ncolonial city center, enjoying the scenery of colonial\narchitecture, churches, and squares. We continue\nto Parque El Paraiso, a beautiful natural area near\ndowntown, then on to San Joaquin, a nearby\nvillage known for its handicrafts and gastronomy.\nAfter lunch and shopping in San Joaquin, we\nmake our way back to Cuenca, riding through\nnarrow streets and colonial neighborhoods. In the\nafternoon, we drive to nearby Baños, a suburb of\nCuenca famous for its natural volcanic hot springs.\nWe spend the rest of the afternoon relaxing in the\nluxurious Piedra de Agua hot springs, where we\nenjoy thermal pools, therapeutic mud baths, and a\ngourmet dinner. (L, D)<br/><br/>Accommodation: Hotel Carvallo Twin and Double Room<br/>',NULL,NULL,'BIKE CUENCA S OLD TOWN, BAÑOS HOT SPRINGS',NULL,'<br/>','jigranda','2016-08-29 13:18:08','jigranda','2016-08-29 13:46:34'),
(62,69,NULL,'en','Today we visit El Cajas National Park, one of\nCuenca´s top natural attractions. This highland\narea features a unique ´´paramo´´ ecosystem, a\nsort of tropical tundra endemic to the northern\nAndes. The paramo in El Cajas is notable for its\nextremely high humidity. The ground is covered\nin sponge-like vegetation and the park is home\nto over 200 lakes and lagoons. Our first stop is\nLaguna Llaviucu, one of the park´s most beautiful\nlagoons. As we hike around Llaviucu, we get\nintroduced to many of the region´s endemic\nspecies. We then carry on to Tres Cruces, the\npark´s highest point at 4,200 meters, where\nwe take in panoramic views of the landscape.\nOur final destination is Laguna La Toreadora,\nwhere we set out on a three-hour hike to\nexplore the small lagoons, beautiful landscapes,\nand endemic flora and fauna surrounding La\nToreadora. On our way back to town, we stop\nat Dos Chorreras, a colonial hosteria where we\nenjoy a hearty lunch of typical dishes, including\nEl Cajas´ famous trout. We return to Cuenca in\nthe late afternoon and enjoy a relaxing evening\nstrolling through town. (B, L, D)<br/><br/>Accommodation: Hotel Carvallo Twin and Double Room<br/>',NULL,NULL,'HIKE EL CAJAS NATIONAL PARK',NULL,'<br/>','jigranda','2016-08-29 13:18:08','jigranda','2016-08-29 13:46:47'),
(63,70,NULL,'en','This morning, we drive into the countryside\nsurrounding Cuenca and on to a nearby colonial\nhacienda. After an introduction to the grounds\nand a short riding lesson, we get on our horses\nand set out for a three-hour ride through the rural\nAndean countryside. We ride at a relaxed pace\nalong beautiful trails, passing through ancient\nvillages, small farms, and idyllic landscapes. After\nour ride, we enjoy a delicious lunch and finish\nour day with a short walk around the hacienda.\nWe drive back to Cuenca in the afternoon and\ncatch our flight back to Quito. (B, L) \n<br/><br/><b>INCLUDED\n</b><br/>Accommodations in boutique hotel, private land\ntransportation, all meals as listed (B=breakfast,\nL=lunch, D=dinner), high-quality biking and riding\nequipment, bilingual naturalist guide.\n<br/><br/><b>NOT INCLUDED\n</b><br/>Round trip airfare to and from Cuenca, hotel\nand restaurant beverages, tips.\n<br/><br/><b>IMPORTANT INFORMATION\n<br/>RECOMMENDED ITEMS TO PACK:</b> Waterproof\nhiking boots, waterproof gaiters, waterproof rain\njacket, warm layered clothing, non-cotton trekking\nclothes, bathing suit, camera, sunscreen,\ninsect repellant.',NULL,NULL,'COLONIAL HACIENDA HORSEBACK RIDE',NULL,'<br/>','jigranda','2016-08-29 13:18:08',NULL,NULL),
