(111,'ECA029','en','Cotopaxi National Park Hike 1 Day','Effort: Moderate. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, wildlife observation.<br>\n<br>\nThe Cotopaxi National Park isWe depart from Quito in the morning and head south, driving through the Avenue of the Volcanoes.Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed eiusmod tempor incidunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquid ex ea commodi consequat.','S','ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:49:40','jmora','2017-07-19 21:34:13'),
(112,'ECA030','es','Guagua Pichincha Volcano Hike 1 Day','Effort: Moderate to challenging. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, nature viewing.<br>\n<br>\nOverlooking Quito, Pichincha Volcano is an ever-present part of the city\'s scenery. The tallest of its three peaks, Guagua Pichincha, stands at 4,874 meters (15,991 ft.) and makes for a spectacular day hike from the city. The dramatic changes in environment from cloud forest to paramo and barren rock make this hike a truly memorable experience.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Enjoy the change from cloud forest to paramo to volcanic rock as you gain elevation.<br>\n* Admire spectacular views during the drive up to the Guagua Pichincha refuge.<br>\n* Learn about the area\'s natural history and\ngeology from your expert guide.<br>\n* Look into the active caldera of Guagua\nPichincha.<br>','N','ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:54:59','ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:57:58'),
(113,'ECA030','en','Guagua Pichincha Volcano Hike 1 Day','Effort: Moderate to challenging. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, nature viewing.<br>\n<br>\nOverlooking Quito, Pichincha Volcano is an ever-present part of the city\'s scenery. The tallest of its three peaks, Guagua Pichincha, stands at 4,874 meters (15,991 ft.) and makes for a spectacular day hike from the city. The dramatic changes in environment from cloud forest to paramo and barren rock make this hike a truly memorable experience.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Enjoy the change from cloud forest to paramo to volcanic rock as you gain elevation.<br>\n* Admire spectacular views during the drive up to the Guagua Pichincha refuge.<br>\n* Learn about the area\'s natural history and\ngeology from your expert guide.<br>\n* Look into the active caldera of Guagua\nPichincha.<br>','N','ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:57:45','ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:57:53'),
(116,'ECA032','es','Pasochoa Protector Forest 1 Day','Effort: Moderate. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, bird watching, nature viewing.<br>\n<br>\nThis wildlife refuge is a humid cloud forest located within the crater of the extinct Pasochoa\nvolcano. Best known for bird watching and its variety of cloud forest ecosystems, the refuge is home to over 100 bird species and 50 species of endemic plants, as well as deer, foxes, and even pumas. Our expert guide will help identify species and interpret the region\'s natural history.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Observe incredible bird life, much of it\nendemic to Ecuador\'s cloud forests.<br>\n* Experience abrupt vegetation changes while\nhiking through different elevations.<br>\n* Keep an eye out for foxes, deer,\nand occasionally the elusive puma.<br>\n* Enjoy the beautiful backdrop of snow-capped volcanoes.<br>','N','ddiaz','2015-03-21 00:20:29','ddiaz','2015-03-21 00:28:42'),
(117,'ECA032','en','Pasochoa Protector Forest 1 Day','Effort: Moderate. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, bird watching, nature viewing.<br>\n<br>\nThis wildlife refuge is a humid cloud forest located within the crater of the extinct Pasochoa\nvolcano. Best known for bird watching and its variety of cloud forest ecosystems, the refuge is home to over 100 bird species and 50 species of endemic plants, as well as deer, foxes, and even pumas. Our expert guide will help identify species and interpret the region\'s natural history.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Observe incredible bird life, much of it\nendemic to Ecuador\'s cloud forests.<br>\n* Experience abrupt vegetation changes while\nhiking through different elevations.<br>\n* Keep an eye out for foxes, deer,\nand occasionally the elusive puma.<br>\n* Enjoy the beautiful backdrop of snow-capped volcanoes.<br>','N','ddiaz','2015-03-21 00:23:11','ddiaz','2015-03-21 00:28:48'),
