('ECA005','0002','Effort: Easy.<br>\nActivities: Bird watching, walking, wildlife encounters, learning.<br>\n<br>\nThe Mindo Cloud Forest Reserve is one of the\nworld\'s true hotspots of biodiversity. Home\nto over 520 species of birds, which account\nfor 5% of the world\'s total bird species, this\nregion is a birdwatcher\'s dream. In addition\nto bird life, Mindo is home to many other\nplant and animal species that thrive in its lush\ncloud forest ecosystem, making the reserve\na beautiful and scenic place to explore.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Walk along a picturesque cloud forest trail\nwith beautiful views.<br>\n* Observe teeming bird life, beautiful orchids\nand bromeliads, and other wildlife.<br>\n* Visit a local waterfall and have lunch\nin the charming town of Mindo.','Mindo Cloud Forest 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','C',NULL,0.7000,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-18 00:52:59','jigranda','2016-08-29 12:50:17'),
('ECA007','0002','Effort: Easy.<br>\nActivities: Spa relaxation, walking, wildlife observation.<br>\n<br>\nPapallacta is located in the midst of\nthe Avenue of the Volcanoes, next to a\nparticularly high-quality natural hot spring.\nTermas de Papallacta Resort and Spa blends\nthe mineral-rich, 150° water to create\nthermal pools of various temperatures.\nThe beautiful setting, quality facilities, and\ncurative waters make for a day of pure\nrelaxation. Optional spa services include\na variety of massages and can be reserved\nin advance.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Relax in curative and comfortable volcanic\nhot springs in a quality spa setting.<br>\n* Explore the cloud forest reserve and search\nfor bird life on a laid-back nature walk.<br>\n* Optional spa services are highly\nrecommended.<br>','Papallacta Hot Springs 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-18 01:18:53','ddiaz','2015-03-18 01:29:49'),
('ECA008','0002','Effort: Easy.<br>\nActivities: Walking, sightseeing, culture learning.<br>\n<br>\nDiscover the highlights of Quito in only\none day! Ecuador\'s capital was declared\nUNESCO\'s first world heritage site in 1972\nand is known for having the best-preserved\ncolonial city center in Latin America.\nSurrounded by rolling hills and looming\nmountains, Quito is a place of natural\nand cultural beauty. Visit the highlights\nof colonial Quito, then travel north to\nexplore the monuments and museums that\nmark Latitude Zero, all with the expert\ninterpretation of our historian guides.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Discover Quito\'s remarkably preserved\ncolonial architecture, churches, and plazas.<br>\n* Explore the largest colonial city center in Latin America.<br>\n* Marvel at the Beauty of Colonial churches.<br>\n* Visit the \'\'Mitad del Mundo\'\' monument.<br>\n* Visit the Intiñan Museum.<br>\n* Stand with one foot in each hemisphere\nat Latitude Zero.<br>','USAR Quito City Tour & Equatorial Monument 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-18 01:34:01','ddiaz','2015-04-08 12:31:02'),
('ECA010','0002','Effort: Moderate, no experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Horseback riding, hiking, and mountain biking.<br>\nAccommodation: Colonial hacienda.<br>\n<br>\nThis exciting tour is the best way to experience\nthe Ecuadorian Andes in just two days. The\narea we will explore, known as the Avenue of\nthe Volcanoes, has one of the world?s highest\nconcentrations of volcanoes over 15,000 ft. (4,800 m). We will explore this spectacular\narea while horseback riding, biking, hiking,\nsearching for Andean condors, exploring Inca\nruins, and learning about Chagra (Andean\ncowboy) culture.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Ride on horseback Chagra-style through\nCotopaxi National Park.<br>\n* Bike down a breathtaking route alongside\nthe Illinizas volcanoes.<br>\n* Search for Andean condors, falcons, deer,\nhares, foxes, and other Andean wildlife.<br>\n* Visit the Pucara ruins and learn about Inca\nhistory in Ecuador.<br>\n* Learn natural history, geology, history, and\nChagra cowboy culture from expert guides.<br>','Avenue of the Volcanoes by Horse and Bike 2 Days',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-18 02:20:11','ddiaz','2015-03-18 02:28:20'),
('ECA019','0002','Effort: Moderate to challenging, no experience necessary.<br>\nActivities:Canopy zip lining, canyoning, cultural exploration.<br>\nAccommodation: Boutique hotel.<br>\n<br>\nFor those seeking the more adventurous\nside of the southern Andes, this tour\nfeatures two of Cuenca?s newest and most\nexciting adventure activities. Blast through\nthe forest canopy on a high-speed zip line\ntour, then rappel, scramble, and swim your\nway through a beautiful, rocky canyon.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Navigate waterfalls, rock slides, and pools as you explore a scenic canyon.<br>\n* Fly through lush forests and enjoy countryside views on a zipline canopy tour.<br>\n* Explore Cuenca?s beautiful, historic old town.<br>','Azuay Valley Canopy & Canyoning 2 Days',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-20 20:53:13','ddiaz','2015-03-20 20:55:40'),
('ECA020','0002','Effort: Moderate, no experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Biking, hiking, horseback riding, cultural exploration, wildlife observation.<br>\nAccommodation:Boutique hotel.<br>\n<br>\nThis multisport tour is a great way to\nactively explore the highlights of laid-back\nCuenca and the southern Andes. Cycle\ndown colonial streets, visit a colonial\nhacienda on horseback, and hike the\nrugged paramo landscape of El Cajas\nNational Park, filled with hundreds of\nsmall lakes and unique wildlife.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Bike through the beautiful colonial center\nof Cuenca, a UNESCO world heritage site.<br>\n* Relax in the natural volcanic hot springs\nof Baños de Cuenca.<br>\n* Hike the rugged paramo landscapes\nof El Cajas National Park.<br>\n* Learn about the traditional hacienda lifestyle\non horseback.<br>','Cuenca and Cajas Multiactive 3 Days',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',10.0000,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-20 21:01:23','jigranda','2016-08-29 13:07:26'),
('ECA021','0002','Effort: Moderate, no experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Rock climbing, biking, cultural exploration.<br>\nAccommodation: Boutique hotel.<br>\n<br>\nJust 30 minutes from the laid-back southern\ncity of Cuenca, Cojitambo is the best\nclimbing site in Ecuador, with quality\nrock, scenic surroundings, and panoramic\nviews from the top. This southern multisport\nadventure combines an exciting day of\nrock climbing with a scenic bike tour of\nCuenca\'s beautiful colonial center.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Bike through the beautiful colonial center\nof Cuenca, a UNESCO world heritage site.<br>\n* Climb at Ecuador\'s best climbing site,\nwith walls up to 60 meters tall.<br>\n* Take in beautiful highland scenery\nand panoramic views as you climb.<br>','Historical Biking and Rock Climbing Adventure 2 Days',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-20 21:18:43','ddiaz','2015-03-20 21:20:50'),
('ECA026','0002','Effort: Moderate to challenging (Class IV). Some rafting experience recommended.<br>\nActivities: Whitewater rafting.<br>\n<br>\nThe Quijos River is the best Class IV run\nthat can be done as a day trip from Quito.\nIt originates from the glaciers of Volcan\nAntisana (5,758 meters) and runs a steep\ndescent towards the Amazon through a\nbeautiful cloud forest filled with bird life.\nThis medium-volume run cuts through the\npicturesque Chaco gorge and is a classic\namong rafters and kayakers alike.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Paddle the best Class IV rapids between\nthe Andes and the Amazon.<br>\n* Enjoy beautiful cloud forest scenery\nin the surrounding Chaco gorge.<br>\n* Cross the continental divide at 4,000 meters\nof altitude.<br>\n* Support raft and kayakers ensure safety\nand provide great riverside service.<br>','Quijos River Rafting 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-20 22:22:07','ddiaz','2015-03-20 22:52:30'),
('ECA029','0002','Effort: Moderate. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, wildlife observation.<br>\n<br>\nThe Cotopaxi National Park isWe depart from Quito in the morning and head south, driving through the Avenue of the Volcanoes.Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed eiusmod tempor incidunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquid ex ea commodi consequat.','Cotopaxi National Park Hike 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:40:22','jmora','2017-07-19 21:34:13'),
('ECA030','0002','Effort: Moderate to challenging. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, nature viewing.<br>\n<br>\nOverlooking Quito, Pichincha Volcano is an ever-present part of the city\'s scenery. The tallest of its three peaks, Guagua Pichincha, stands at 4,874 meters (15,991 ft.) and makes for a spectacular day hike from the city. The dramatic changes in environment from cloud forest to paramo and barren rock make this hike a truly memorable experience.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Enjoy the change from cloud forest to paramo to volcanic rock as you gain elevation.<br>\n* Admire spectacular views during the drive up to the Guagua Pichincha refuge.<br>\n* Learn about the area\'s natural history and\ngeology from your expert guide.<br>\n* Look into the active caldera of Guagua\nPichincha.<br>','Guagua Pichincha Volcano Hike 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:54:59','ddiaz','2015-03-20 23:57:26'),
('ECA032','0002','Effort: Moderate. No experience necessary.<br>\nActivities: Hiking, bird watching, nature viewing.<br>\n<br>\nThis wildlife refuge is a humid cloud forest located within the crater of the extinct Pasochoa\nvolcano. Best known for bird watching and its variety of cloud forest ecosystems, the refuge is home to over 100 bird species and 50 species of endemic plants, as well as deer, foxes, and even pumas. Our expert guide will help identify species and interpret the region\'s natural history.<br>\n<br>\nTrip highlights:<br>\n* Observe incredible bird life, much of it\nendemic to Ecuador\'s cloud forests.<br>\n* Experience abrupt vegetation changes while\nhiking through different elevations.<br>\n* Keep an eye out for foxes, deer,\nand occasionally the elusive puma.<br>\n* Enjoy the beautiful backdrop of snow-capped volcanoes.<br>','Pasochoa Protector Forest 1 Day',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','T',NULL,NULL,NULL,'I','S','U',NULL,NULL,'N','S',NULL,'N','N',NULL,'SRV','N',NULL,NULL,'ddiaz','2015-03-21 00:20:29','ddiaz','2015-03-21 00:28:37'),
